Upstream tools

The conversion and benchmark use turboderp-org/exllamav3, distributed under the
MIT License:

    https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3

The scripts here call exllamav3 as an installed dependency and do not vendor or
copy its source. The EXL3 trellis method builds on QTIP.

Benchmark inputs

The input windows are built by bench/build_inputs.py from one public-domain book
in the PG-19 test split (DeepMind, Apache-2.0) and the src/*.cpp files of
llama.cpp (MIT). The token ids are not redistributed in this repository; only the
builder and SHA-256 checksums are published. The upstream licenses for those
sources continue to apply.
